    {
      "text": "seek ye first the kingdom of God, Matt. 6:33 (3 Ne. 13:33). last state … is worse than the first, Matt. 12:45 (Luke 11:26). Elias must first come, Matt. 17:10 (Mark 9:11). first shall be last; and the last shall be first, Matt. 19:30 (Mark 10:31). last shall be first, and the first last, Matt. 20:16 (Luke 13:30; 1 Ne. 13:42; Ether 13:12; D&C 29:30). first and great commandment, Matt. 22:38 (Mark 12:30). last error shall be worse than the first, Matt. 27:64. first day of the week, Matt. 28:1 (Mark 16:2; Luke 24:1; John 20:1, 19; Acts 20:7; 1 Cor. 16:2). desire to be first, the same shall be last, Mark 9:35. without sin among you, let him first cast a stone, John 8:7. disciples were called Christians first in Antioch, Acts 11:26. Christ … first that should rise from the dead, Acts 26:23. Jew first, and also to the Greek, Rom. 1:16 (2:9–10). first man Adam was made a living soul, 1 Cor. 15:45. that was not first which is spiritual, 1 Cor. 15:46 (D&C 128:14). who first trusted in Christ, Eph. 1:12. he also descended first into the lower parts, Eph. 4:9. the first commandment with promise, Eph. 6:2. dead in Christ shall rise first, 1 Thes. 4:16. except there come a falling away first, 2 Thes. 2:3. if that first covenant had been faultless, Heb. 8:7. first covenant had also ordinances of divine service, Heb. 9:1. We love him, because he first loved us, 1 Jn. 4:19. angels which kept not their first estate, Jude 1:6. because thou hast left thy first love, Rev. 2:4. This is the first resurrection, Rev. 20:5.",
